    "chunks": [
      "2 - Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn al-Walid (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated to us... from Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ali al-Baqir (peace be upon them both). He said:",
      "The name of the Messenger of Allah in the Scrolls of Ibrahim is al-Mahi, in the Torah al-Hadd, in the Gospel Ahmad, in the Quran Muhammad. Al-Mahi effaces the images of idols. Al-Hadd opposes Allah's enemies. Ahmad is God's beautiful praise. Muhammad is praised by Allah, His angels, prophets and nations, and his name is on the Throne.",
      "He would wear Yemeni and white skullcaps, and padded ones with ear-flaps in wartime. He had a staff, a spear called al-Mamshūq, a tent called al-Kinn, bowls, cups, two horses, two mules (Duldul and al-Shahba'), two she-camels, swords (Dhulfiqar and others), a donkey Ya'fur, a turban al-Sahab, armor Dhat al-Fudul with silver rings, a flag al-'Uqab, a camel al-Dibaj, a banner al-Ma'lum, and a helmet al-As'ad.",
      "He handed all of these to Ali (peace be upon him) at his death, took off his ring and placed it on Ali's finger. Ali mentioned finding a parchment in one of his swords with three phrases: 'Maintain ties with those who cut you off, speak the truth even against yourself, and be good to those who wrong you.'",
      "He said: And the Messenger of Allah said: There are five things I will not abandon until death: eating on the ground with slaves, riding donkeys without saddles, milking goats by hand, wearing wool, and greeting children so that it may be a tradition after me."
    ],
